+ * - The control's defaults: binary messages, whole messages, no size limit,
+ *   65536 bytes of outbound buffer, a 30 second pong interval; the protocols
+ *   asked for go in Sec-WebSocket-Protocol and the one the server chose is
+ *   the information's Protocol.
+ * - The information object exists from the start and is the same object
+ *   after the connection, which fills in the local address and protocol.
+ * - The output stream exists from the start too and is the same object
+ *   every time; each WriteAsync is one whole message, text or binary as the
+ *   control says at the time, sent in the order written.  IMessageWebSocket3
+ *   sends a message in frames.
+ * - A message arrives whole unless the receive mode is PartialMessage; its
+ *   DataReader, the same one each time it is asked for, starts out holding
+ *   the whole message, and its input stream reads the message again from the
+ *   start.
+ * - Close sends the close frame, with the status given or, from IClosable,
+ *   empty; writing or connecting afterwards fails at once with RO_E_CLOSED.
+ *   Closed is raised when the server answers, with its code and reason, or
+ *   with 1006 if the connection ends without an answer.  A status no close
+ *   frame may carry, or a reason longer than 123 bytes of UTF-8, is refused
+ *   with E_INVALIDARG and the socket stays as it was.
+ * - A close frame from the server raises Closed as well, and leaves this
+ *   side free to write until it closes in turn.
+ * - A connection that ends with no close frame either way, or on the
+ *   server breaking the protocol, raises no Closed: a last MessageReceived
+ *   carries the error, 0x80072efe or 0x80072f78, which reading its data
+ *   returns, and every later write fails with 0x80072efe.  Close then sends
+ *   nothing and raises Closed with 1006 before it returns.
+ * - A server that does not upgrade fails the connection with its status as
+ *   an HRESULT, 0x80190000 + status.
  */
 
